.IX Title "Clownfish::Err 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::Err 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::Err \- Exception.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    package MyErr;
\&    use base qw( Clownfish::Err );
\&    
\&    ...
\&    
\&    package main;
\&    use Scalar::Util qw( blessed );
\&    while (1) {
\&        eval {
\&            do_stuff() or MyErr\->throw("retry");
\&        };
\&        if ( blessed($@) and $@\->isa("MyErr") ) {
\&            warn "Retrying...\en";
\&        }
\&        else {
\&            # Re\-throw.
\&            die "do_stuff() died: $@";
\&        }
\&    }
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Clownfish::Err is the base class for exceptions in the Clownfish object
hierarchy.
.PP
The Err module also provides access to a per-thread Err shared variable via
\&\fBset_error()\fR and \fBget_error()\fR.  It may be used to store an Err object
temporarily, so that calling code may choose how to handle a particular
error condition.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS cat_mess
.IX Subsection "cat_mess"
.Vb 1
\&    $err\->cat_mess($mess);
.Ve
.PP
Concatenate the supplied argument onto the error message.
.SS get_mess
.IX Subsection "get_mess"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $err\->get_mess();
.Ve
.PP
Return the error message.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::Err isa Clownfish::Obj.
